Implemented the Track B generator based on the [full arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1105.5509).

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1105.5509/gen_1105_5509.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1105.5509/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1105.5509/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1105.5509/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1105.5509/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1105.5509/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- G9 size caps pass: 771 characters, 96 elements, 286 intended operations.
- Uniform guessing: 0/200,000.
- Six heuristic attacks: 0/8 each.
- Reference Gauss–Jordan algorithm: 8/8, about 17,000 field operations.
- All 59 `gvlib` tests pass.

The result is not yet releasable: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “key total limit exceeded” for all three harness runs, leaving zero scored oracle attempts. G9 and the required hardness verdict are therefore honestly marked pending rather than inferred from API failures. No `REJECTED.md` was written because this is an infrastructure block, not a mathematical rejection.
